{"findings":[{"finding":"2 — AC-17.3 only records an unsuccessful set-inactive request when the indicator integration is unavailable, so the spec neither ensures the green indicator becomes inactive nor defines a retry or safe fallback despite requiring inactivity on every verification failure.","reqId":"REQ-17","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"1 — REQ-19 creates utilization events for configured working days, but REQ-20 calculates the weekly denominator across the Monday-through-Sunday reporting week without excluding non-working days, so the reported percentage can include allocations with no corresponding utilization event.","reqId":"REQ-20","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"3 — AC-15.1 requires processing a recorded stickered-vehicle arrival, but no requirement defines a public interface or event source that records that arrival, leaving this acceptance criterion untestable at the specified app surface.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"2 — AC-3.2 tests an active employee saving a vehicle but never verifies that the employee can only add or edit their own plates, leaving the assumed self-service vehicle flow without an observable authorization boundary for employee vehicle data.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"2 — REQ-18 requires recording every unsuccessful entrance-verification attempt, but its acceptance criterion covers only a verification that succeeds or fails after processing and does not establish audit records for rejected unauthenticated or replayed requests described in REQ-16.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"}]}